      "key": {
        "uuid": "e5b71404_b821f1d1",
        "filename": "include/core/SkPath.h",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1950,
      "author": {
        "id": 5648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-26T20:07:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmmm, actually we rarely do that in the sk_sp\u003c\u003e. Look at SkPaint.h -- all of its many fields are logically const (e.g. shader, blender, etc.), but that is a property of the class itself, not the sk_sp holder.",
      "parentUuid": "7f58c854_c7aef15f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1950,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 1950,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "20f8056b781c5bd493459210c0da5a54a7724e23",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "119f92bc_5ba6c75e",
        "filename": "include/core/SkPath.h",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1950,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-29T17:09:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I know we rarely *have done* it, but I\u0027m also a fan of calling out const for data like things even though it\u0027s sort of implicit. https://review.skia.org/1084037. So let\u0027s add it in here now.",
      "parentUuid": "e5b71404_b821f1d1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1950,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 1950,
        "endChar": 20
      },
      "revId": "20f8056b781c5bd493459210c0da5a54a7724e23",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "df883a22_5f98e0c5",
        "filename": "include/core/SkPath.h",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 1950,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-10-29T18:25:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Consistency with other implicitly immutable Skia types (shaders, color filters, etc) is a good point though.  It makes sense to keep things aligned, and we don\u0027t have to make a decision right now.  Let\u0027s chat internally about what we want to do with those, and apply globally.",
      "parentUuid": "119f92bc_5ba6c75e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1950,
        "startChar": 10,
        "endLine": 1950,
        "endChar": 20
      },
